  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "How a Response is Generated by Effectors"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- The nervous system enables the body to **detect changes in the environment **and brings about **appropriate responses** to ensure its safety\n\n  - **Receptor cells** detect changes in the environment, or **stimuli**\n  - Nerve impulses travel from the receptor cells along **sensory neurones **to the **central nervous system,** or CNS\n  - The **CNS **acts as a **coordinating centre** for the impulses that arrive from the receptors, determining which part of the body needs to respond and sending out a new set of impulses along **motor neurones**\n  - **Motor neurones send impulses** to the** effectors **to bring about a **response**\n  \n    - Effectors may be muscles or glands\n- Nerve impulses pass through the nervous system along the following pathway"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "**stimulus **$\\rightarrow$** receptor **$\\rightarrow$** sensory neurone **$\\rightarrow$** CNS **$\\rightarrow$**motor neurone **$\\rightarrow$**effector**"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2021/07/Nerve-pathway-stimulus-to-response.png",
   "file": "assets/92700dd5e625-nerve-pathway-stimulus-to-response.png",
   "alt": "Nerve pathway stimulus to response",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "***Receptors detect stimuli and impulses are sent through to the nervous system to bring about a response in the effector***"
  }
 ]
